content.text:
This round's refactoring is complete and verified. Here's a summary.

## This round: two more structural improvements

Building on the earlier offspring-polymorphism refactor, I tackled the two biggest remaining smells in the `Animal` hierarchy.

### 1. Pull up duplicated constructor bodies (`Prey`/`Predator`)
The five concrete species had near-identical constructors — the same stat-assignment block plus the same `randomAge`/newborn-food initialization, copy-pasted with only the constants varying. I moved that logic into enriched `Prey` and `Predator` superclass constructors that take the species stats as parameters. Each species constructor is now a one-line `super(...)` call:

```java
public Lion(boolean randomAge, Field field, Location location, boolean isInfected, boolean isImmune) {
    super(randomAge, field, location, isInfected, isImmune,
          PREY_CATCHING_PROBABILITY, BREEDING_AGE, MAX_AGE, BREEDING_PROBABILITY,
          MAX_LITTER_SIZE, MAX_FOOD_LEVEL, FOOD_VALUE);
}
```

The prey/predator distinction (fixed `NEWBORN_FOOD_FRACTION` for prey vs. random `rand.nextDouble()/5.5` for predators) now lives in the right place — the respective superclass. Public constructor signatures are unchanged.

### 2. Extract Method on `Animal.act()` + remove dead code
The ~85-line `act()` method mixed five concerns into one block. Split into intention-revealing helpers:

```java
public void act(List<LivingOrganism> newAnimals) {
    incrementAge();
    incrementHunger();
    updateInfectionState();
    if (isAlive()) {
        tryToCatchDisease();
        tryToBreed(newAnimals);
        move();
    }
}
```

Also removed a dead no-op in `setDead()` (an `if (class == Lion || Cheetah) location = null;` block that ran only after `location` was already nulled).

## Verification
The simulation is non-deterministic by default (`Randomizer.useShared = false`), so I used the headless harness that reflectively seeds the three RNG instances and fingerprints position-sensitive per-step field state. **All four configurations** (default plus three seed/step/grid variations, up to 200 steps) produce **byte-identical fingerprints between the pristine baseline (commit `298c765`) and the fully refactored tree** — confirming every change preserves exact behavior. The full tree compiles cleanly (24 classes).

Cumulative design changes vs. the original baseline:

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `Animal.java` | offspring polymorphism, `act()` extraction, dead-code removal |
| `Prey.java`, `Predator.java` | enriched constructors absorbing per-species init |
| `Lion`, `Cheetah`, `Zebra`, `Giraffe`, `Lemur` | one-line constructors + `createOffspring` overrides |

Net: substantial duplication removed, conditional-on-type dispatch eliminated, and the longest method decomposed — with behavior provably unchanged.

